00:00:52,420 --> 00:00:57,820
In Britain, on the 26th of December,

12
00:00:58,520 --> 00:01:06,900
the day after Christmas, the very rich people in Victorian times gave gifts to their

13
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:09,260
servants in small boxes.

14
00:01:09,260 --> 00:01:14,020
That's why it was called Boxing Day.

15
00:01:15,440 --> 00:01:22,380
Another possibility is that the name refers to money that was given to people in

16
00:01:22,380 --> 00:01:29,120
need. Traditionally, a box was placed in churches to collect money.

17
00:01:29,900 --> 00:01:36,200
The money from the box was given out to the poor on the day after Christmas.

